  'revision.exam_technique.breadcrumb_label': 'Exam Technique',
  'revision.exam_technique.back_to_hub': 'Back to Revision Hub',
  'revision.exam_technique.page_title': '{board} Exam Technique',
  'revision.exam_technique.page_subtitle':
    'Essay structure, timing and marking guide mastery for {board}',
  'revision.exam_technique.why_matters_badge': 'Why This Matters',
  'revision.exam_technique.why_matters_heading':
    'Technique can be the difference between Grade 5 and Grade 9',
  'revision.exam_technique.why_matters_body':
    'You can know every quote and every context point, but without strong exam technique your knowledge stays in your head instead of on the page. These guides are tailored specifically to the {board} specification - paper structures, question types and what each grade looks like - so every tip maps to the marks you can actually earn.',
  'revision.exam_technique.guides_heading': '{board} Technique Guides',
  'revision.exam_technique.read_guide': 'Read guide',
  'revision.exam_technique.quick_tips_heading': 'Quick Tips',
  'revision.exam_technique.markers_heading': 'Know What Your {board} Markers Look For',
  'revision.exam_technique.markers_body':
    'Every mark in GCSE English is tied to what markers look for. AOs differ between Literature and Language papers - Literature uses AO1-AO4, while Language uses AO1-AO4 (reading) and AO5-AO6 (writing). Note that AO4 means different things in each.',
  'revision.exam_technique.guide.essay_structure.title': 'Essay Structure',
  'revision.exam_technique.guide.essay_structure.desc':
    'PEEL paragraphs, thesis statements, introductions, conclusions and model answers aligned to what each {board} grade looks like.',
  'revision.exam_technique.guide.essay_structure.tag': 'Essential',
  'revision.exam_technique.guide.time_management.title': 'Time Management',
  'revision.exam_technique.guide.time_management.desc':
    'Minute-by-minute plans for every {board} paper, marks-to-time conversion and rapid planning techniques.',
  'revision.exam_technique.guide.question_types.title': 'Question Types',
  'revision.exam_technique.guide.question_types.desc':
    'Every {board} question type decoded - how to approach extract, comparison, creative and evaluation questions.',
  'revision.exam_technique.tip.read_question.title': 'Read the question twice',
  'revision.exam_technique.tip.read_question.body':
    'Underline key command words and circle the focus of the question before you start writing. Most marks are lost through misreading, not poor knowledge.',
  'revision.exam_technique.tip.plan.title': 'Plan for 5 minutes',
  'revision.exam_technique.tip.plan.body':
    'A rough plan prevents waffle and keeps your argument focused. Jot down 3 points, the quotes you will use, and your thesis before writing.',
  'revision.exam_technique.tip.embed_quotes.title': 'Embed your quotes',
  'revision.exam_technique.tip.embed_quotes.body':
    'Never drop a quote into a sentence on its own. Weave it into your analysis: "Shelley uses the adjective \'vast\' to convey..." is far stronger than a standalone quote.',
  'revision.exam_technique.tip.link_ideas.title': 'Link to the big ideas',
  'revision.exam_technique.tip.link_ideas.body':
    'Markers reward responses that connect to context, authorial intent, and wider themes. Always ask yourself: why did the writer make this choice?',
  'revision.exam_technique.tip.watch_clock.title': 'Watch the clock',
  'revision.exam_technique.tip.watch_clock.body':
    'If you cannot finish a paragraph, write your key point in a single sentence and move on. A complete paper with short answers beats an incomplete paper with perfect ones.',
  'revision.exam_technique.tip.terminology.title': 'Use subject terminology',
  'revision.exam_technique.tip.terminology.body':
    'Words like "metaphor", "sibilance", "iambic pentameter", and "semantic field" show the marker you understand craft. Use them precisely, not just to drop them in.',
  'revision.exam_technique.ao.response_quotation.label': 'Response & quotation',
  'revision.exam_technique.ao.response_quotation.detail':
    'Lit & Lang: read, understand, and respond using textual references (including quotations) to support your interpretation.',
  'revision.exam_technique.ao.language_structure.label': 'Language & structure',
  'revision.exam_technique.ao.language_structure.detail':
    'Lit & Lang: analyse how writers use language, form, and structure to create meanings and effects. Use relevant subject terminology.',
  'revision.exam_technique.ao.context_synthesis.label': 'Context (Lit) / Synthesis (Lang)',
  'revision.exam_technique.ao.context_synthesis.detail':
    "Lit: show understanding of texts and the contexts they were written in. Lang: compare writers' ideas and perspectives across two or more texts.",
  'revision.exam_technique.ao.ao4_lit.label': 'Technical accuracy',
  'revision.exam_technique.ao.ao4_lit.detail':
    'Literature only: use a range of vocabulary and sentence structures for clarity, purpose and effect with accurate spelling and punctuation. Worth ~5% of Lit marks and assessed on specific essays only (e.g. AQA Shakespeare + modern text).',
  'revision.exam_technique.ao.ao4_lang.label': 'Evaluation',
  'revision.exam_technique.ao.ao4_lang.detail':
    'Language reading only: evaluate texts critically, supporting this with appropriate textual references.',
  'revision.exam_technique.ao.ao5.label': 'Writing: content & organisation',
  'revision.exam_technique.ao.ao5.detail':
    'Language writing only: communicate clearly, effectively, and imaginatively, selecting and adapting tone, style, and register. Usually 24 of the 40 writing marks.',
  'revision.exam_technique.ao.ao6.label': 'Writing: technical accuracy',
  'revision.exam_technique.ao.ao6.detail':
    'Language writing only: use a range of vocabulary and sentence structures for clarity, purpose, and effect with accurate spelling and punctuation. Usually 16 of the 40 writing marks.',
  'revision.exam_technique.cta_heading': 'Start with {board} essay structure',
  'revision.exam_technique.cta_body':
    'Learning how to structure a paragraph properly is the single fastest way to improve your grade. Start with PEEL and work through our {board}-specific model answers.',
  'revision.exam_technique.cta_button': 'Essay Structure Guide',
