  'resources.eng_lit.hub.h1': 'English Literature',
  'resources.eng_lit.hub.for_board': 'For',
  'resources.eng_lit.hub.subtitle':
    'In-depth study guides for Shakespeare, prose, drama, and poetry. Character analysis, theme breakdowns, key quotations, essay techniques, and exam preparation - everything you need in one place.',
  'resources.eng_lit.stat.texts': 'Set Texts Covered',
  'resources.eng_lit.stat.quotes': 'Key Quotations',
  'resources.eng_lit.stat.notes': 'Revision Notes',
  'resources.eng_lit.stat.questions': 'Practice Questions',
  'resources.eng_lit.what.h2': 'What does GCSE English Literature involve?',
  'resources.eng_lit.what.body':
    'GCSE English Literature requires you to read, analyse, and respond to a range of literary texts from different periods and genres. You will develop skills in close reading, critical analysis, comparison, and essay writing - demonstrating how writers create meaning through language, form, and structure. These skills are universal across all exam boards; while the specific texts and paper structures vary, the core analytical approach remains the same.',
  'resources.eng_lit.guides.h2': 'Set text study guides',
  'resources.eng_lit.guides.sub':
    'Detailed revision guides covering plot, characters, themes, key quotations, context, and essay planning. Each guide works for any exam board studying that text.',
  'resources.eng_lit.guides.view': 'View study guide',
  'resources.eng_lit.poetry.h2': 'Poetry anthology guides',
  'resources.eng_lit.poetry.sub':
    'Poem-by-poem analysis with stanza breakdowns, technique identification, thematic links, and comparison pairs.',
  'resources.eng_lit.essay.h2': 'How to write a top-mark literature essay',
  'resources.eng_lit.essay.sub':
    'These techniques apply across all exam boards and question types. Master them and you will consistently reach the higher mark bands.',
  'resources.eng_lit.example.h2': 'Example analytical paragraph',
  'resources.eng_lit.example.sub':
    'See how all six essay tips come together in a single paragraph that would score in the top mark band.',
  'resources.eng_lit.example.question_label': 'Question:',
  'resources.eng_lit.example.effective_label': 'What makes this effective:',
  'resources.eng_lit.ai.h2': 'Get AI-powered essay feedback',
  'resources.eng_lit.ai.sub':
    'Paste your literature essay and receive instant, detailed feedback on your argument, use of evidence, analysis of language, and exam technique. Our AI marker is calibrated to GCSE marking guides.',
  'resources.eng_lit.ai.cta': 'Try it free',
  'resources.eng_lit.more.h2': 'More revision resources',
  'resources.eng_lit.more.sub': 'Strengthen specific skills that markers reward most highly.',
