  'mkt.eal.games.heading': 'English games for beginners',
  'mkt.eal.games.lead':
    '18+ friendly games: picture-word match, articles, the verb “to be”, tenses, prepositions, numbers & time, phrasal verbs and more - with instant feedback and scores.',
  'mkt.eal.games.play_now': 'Play now',
  'mkt.eal.howto.heading': 'How to use this section',
  'mkt.eal.howto.step1.bold': 'Start with the placement test',
  'mkt.eal.howto.step1.body': 'so you know your A2-C1 level and go straight to the right lessons.',
  'mkt.eal.howto.step2.bold': 'Then move to “Sentence Structure”',
  'mkt.eal.howto.step2.body': 'the biggest gap between Arabic and English. Fix word order first.',
  'mkt.eal.howto.step3.bold': 'Next, “Grammar”',
  'mkt.eal.howto.step3.body':
    'articles, tenses, subject-verb agreement - these decide a big chunk of the SPaG grade.',
  'mkt.eal.howto.step4.bold': 'Use “Common Errors” as a checklist',
  'mkt.eal.howto.step4.body':
    'run through it before submitting any essay, and do the exercises and AI assessment in each lesson.',
  'mkt.biz.badge': 'For organisations',
  'mkt.biz.heading': 'English practice and IELTS preparation for staff and learner cohorts',
  'mkt.biz.lead':
    'If your organisation needs to move a group of adults or students up the CEFR ladder, or get them ready to sit IELTS, you can run that on The English Hub today. This page sets out exactly what that includes, and exactly what it does not.',
  'mkt.biz.cta_primary': 'Enquire about a cohort',
  'mkt.biz.cta_secondary': 'Try the CEFR placement test',
  'mkt.biz.scope.title': 'Read this first: what this platform actually is',
  'mkt.biz.scope.body':
    'The English Hub was built for 13-18 year olds sitting GCSE and IGCSE English, and for the schools that teach them. Two parts of it transfer directly to organisations: IELTS preparation, which is an adult exam, and structured EAL practice graded to CEFR levels. Everything offered on this page is one of those two. There is no separate business-communication, workplace-writing or industry-vocabulary library behind it, and we are not going to imply there is.',
  'mkt.biz.caps.heading': 'What your learners get',
  'mkt.biz.caps.lead':
    'Three capabilities, all of them live on the platform now. You can open the first two yourself before you speak to anyone.',
  'mkt.biz.cap.eal.title': 'Structured EAL practice, graded A2 to C1',
  'mkt.biz.cap.eal.desc':
    '{topics} topic units covering sentence building, grammar, vocabulary, pronunciation and the errors that recur most often. Each unit carries worked examples and practice exercises with written explanations ({exercises} exercise sets in total), and splits into reading, listening, writing and speaking work at the learner’s own CEFR band. The material was written for Arabic first-language learners, so the error analysis is sharpest for that group.',
  'mkt.biz.cap.placement.title': 'CEFR placement test',
  'mkt.biz.cap.placement.desc':
    'A placement test that puts each learner on the CEFR ladder from A1 to C2, with per-skill sub-scores and a recommended set of starting topics. The score is calculated deterministically, not by AI, so the same answers always produce the same level. It is free and needs no subscription, which makes it a sensible first step before you commit to anything.',
  'mkt.biz.cap.ielts.title': 'IELTS preparation with AI band feedback',
  'mkt.biz.cap.ielts.desc':
    'Academic and General Training, across all four papers, with a diagnostic, lessons, practice and model answers. Written responses are assessed against the four IELTS criteria and returned with a band for each criterion plus an overall band on the standard half-band scale; spoken responses get the same treatment. The feedback is generated by AI against published assessment criteria. It is practice feedback, not a mark from a registered IELTS examiner, and it is not an official band score.',
  'mkt.biz.cap.eal.link': 'Open the EAL topic list',
  'mkt.biz.cap.placement.link': 'Take the placement test yourself',
  'mkt.biz.cap.ielts.link': 'Open the IELTS section',
  'mkt.biz.cap.fairuse':
    'Fair use on AI feedback: up to 10 assessed writing submissions and 30 assessed speaking responses per learner per day.',
  'mkt.biz.cohort.heading': 'What the person running the programme sees',
  'mkt.biz.cohort.body':
    'An organisation account groups learners into cohorts. It is the same cohort model schools use, so it is the part of the product that has had the most use.',
  'mkt.biz.cohort.point1':
    'Cohorts with join codes, so learners enrol themselves instead of you emailing a spreadsheet of personal data.',
  'mkt.biz.cohort.point2':
    'Three roles: administrator, programme lead and tutor. A tutor sees only the cohorts assigned to them, not the whole organisation.',
  'mkt.biz.cohort.point3':
    'A cohort view of CEFR placement results and activity, so you can see the spread of levels you are dealing with before you plan anything.',
  'mkt.biz.cohort.caveat':
    'Reporting covers what learners do on this platform. It is not a record of their English anywhere else, and it is not a competency assessment for HR purposes.',
  'mkt.biz.excl.heading': 'What is not included',
  'mkt.biz.excl.lead':
    'Better you know now than after a purchase order. None of the following exists today:',
  'mkt.biz.excl.item1':
    'No live teaching, tutoring or classroom delivery. Learning is self-paced with automated feedback.',
  'mkt.biz.excl.item2':
    'No single sign-on, SAML or automated user provisioning. Learners create their own account and join with a code.',
  'mkt.biz.excl.item3':
    'No LMS integration. There is no SCORM package, no LTI tile and no xAPI feed.',
  'mkt.biz.excl.item4':
    'No business-English, workplace-writing or sector-specific vocabulary content. The material is general English, GCSE and IGCSE English, and IELTS.',
  'mkt.biz.excl.item5':
    'No accredited qualification and no official test result. AI band feedback is practice feedback and cannot be used as evidence of English proficiency.',
  'mkt.biz.excl.item6':
    'No self-serve bulk checkout on this site, and no published volume discount. Cohorts are set up by enquiry.',
  'mkt.biz.pricing.heading': 'Pricing, stated plainly',
  'mkt.biz.pricing.ielts':
    'IELTS access is sold per learner at the published rate: £{monthly} a month or £{annual} a year. That is the same price an individual pays.',
  'mkt.biz.pricing.eal':
    'The EAL topic material and the CEFR placement test are open to any account at no cost. AI assessment of writing and speaking against CEFR levels sits behind a paid plan.',
  'mkt.biz.pricing.volume':
    'We do not publish a volume discount, so there is not one quoted here. If you need a purchase order, a single invoice for a cohort or a phased rollout, put it in the enquiry and we will tell you what we can and cannot do.',
  'mkt.biz.pricing.link': 'See all plans on the pricing page',
  'mkt.biz.next.heading': 'What happens after you enquire',
  'mkt.biz.next.step1':
    'Your enquiry goes to the same inbox as our school enquiries, and we reply within one UK working day.',
  'mkt.biz.next.step2':
    'We ask what the cohort actually needs: how many learners, roughly what level they are, and what they need English for. If the honest answer is workplace communication coaching, we will say so and point you elsewhere.',
  'mkt.biz.next.step3':
    'If it is a fit, we agree a small first cohort, set up the organisation account and cohorts, and give you the join codes.',
  'mkt.biz.next.step4':
    'Learners sit the CEFR placement test first, so the starting level is measured rather than assumed.',
  'mkt.biz.form.heading': 'Enquire about a cohort',
